boot/fstab.qcom derives from Fairphone vendor/fairphone/fps
revision 51648f54c2a7d31fc24833adcae3758cb251966f, default/fstab.qcom,
and the corresponding FP6.QREL.16.100.0 EU vendor ramdisk configuration.
Upstream: https://gerrit-public.fairphone.software/vendor/fairphone/fps
Copyright (c) 2019-2020 The Linux Foundation. All rights reserved.
The full upstream redistribution conditions and disclaimer are preserved in
boot/fstab.qcom and apply to that file; LICENSE does not relicense it.

Downstream changes: retain the shipped early /odm/persist mount, identify the
FP6 configuration and remove the optional Google GSI public-key fallback list.
Partition paths, filesystem options and encryption parameters retain their
upstream meaning. No upstream author attribution has been removed.

boot/init.recovery.qcom.rc adapts the Linux Foundation recovery initialization
published in CalyxOS/device_fairphone_FP6 at
 d2c4950eff6d99fc6473419fbbd0b55d42ec9035,
rootdir/etc/init.recovery.qcom.rc. The original BSD redistribution notice is
retained. The adaptation selects the matched FP6 USB controller, bounds waits,
uses the platform recovery's gadget compositions and leaves brightness control
to the recovery UI. Recovery UI geometry and pixel-format settings were compared
with that same device configuration; runtime validation remains required.

The recovery package/property selection in device.mk is derived from
build/make/target/product/base_vendor.mk at GrapheneOS platform_build commit
7f0398241bc8c4ef5255a8063befa5045e5cfab4. Copyright (C) 2018 The Android
Open Source Project, Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE). The selection omits the
unrelated vendor group and adds fastbootd for dynamic-partition recovery.
